            "review_title": "Review at Guiga BBQ",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n1\nGreat variety of Korean dishes, free drinks and sides, good prices and flavors\nSep 2025 • Family\nWe'd been missing Budae jjigae (Korean army stew) since our favourite Budae jjigae restaurant closed, and was pleased to be able to find this here.\n\nIt was Saturday lunchtime and the restaurant was rather empty. Maybe they're busier in the evenings because... they seem to have dozens of dishes great for families and big groups! We liked the \"Beef Loin and Webfoot Octopus Hotplate\" because of its pretty hotplate with three sauces - the kids loved dipping octopus in the melty cheese and the red sauce in the middle wasn't too spicy for them too.\n\nIt was also cool that they have:\n- free flow self-serve ice cream (more than six flavors)\n- free flow drinks (recommend the healthy hot Korean barley tea better for digestion)\n- free banchan, steamed egg, rice\nAll of the above came up to just 420,000vnd (less than 20usd) for four persons! We were so full we still had extra leftover for at least another person.\n\nHowever, the ice-cream all seemed a little hardened - perhaps they should tweak the temperature of the freezer or get fresher tubs of ice-cream?\nRead more\nWritten November 18, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
